# run-hook.cmd is a cmd.exe / bash polyglot. The batch half needs CRLF,
# because cmd.exe goto label parsing is unreliable in a bare-LF file, so
# pin the checked-out bytes on every platform rather than leaving them to
# each client's core.autocrlf. The Unix half re-executes a CR-stripped
# copy of itself, so CRLF is safe for bash as well.
hooks/run-hook.cmd text eol=crlf
